+# NativeGsTextFootprint (N9c)
+
+Development-only AutoCAD 2020 / R23.1 x64 ARX. `BCE_TEST_RUN` synchronously creates an owned in-memory database, one persistent point control, one k3DDrawing GS kernel/model/offscreen device/view. The owned view uses an explicit custom value style and orthographic XY camera: invisible faces, drawable-color edges without edge modifiers, opaque, no lighting/transparency, fixed width/display mask. Sixteen requested/read-back trait values and operations are retained; active properties require exact equality. Face lighting quality/color/opacity are marked inapplicable only when both sides explicitly use kInvisible/kSet (SDK: faces are not drawn). Kernel createView/device.add pairs with eraseAll/device.erase/kernel.deleteView, including a just-attached-before-style/camera exception regression. The kernel request follows the local 2020 SDK ARXDBG sample. There is one fixed request and no fallback loop. No working/current database switch, GUI view, DWG save, shared GS/profile modification, Plot, Python, or external converter occurs in the native command.
+
+The candidate uses `createAutoCADModel` and `kernel.associate(ownedDb, model, kMain)`; the association is only an attempted route. The sole scene graph root is the owned modelspace AcDbBlockTableRecord containing only the exact point marker; only that marker is overruled. Every genuine WorldDraw independently records and checks its context database, entity database/ObjectId and model binding before drawing. An actual mismatch fails and is preserved in `gs-trace.jsonl`; it does not establish impossibility of other public routes. The finite custom value style is copied into an AcDbVisualStyle in this same owned database's style dictionary, closed/reopened and copied back with strict equality of all sixteen raw values/operations. The owned BTR/model is added before setting the owned style ObjectId, as the 2020 ObjectId-overload contract requires. ObjectId/database and reopened persistent source are checked initially and after every frame's erase/readd. A false value-getter return is observation unavailable (actual values/operations are null), not a contradictory default output or a requirement that this other overload resolve the ID; it makes no renderer-consistency claim. A true value-getter observation must meet the active contract. A real contradiction permits only the explicit unqualified lifecycle2 nontext diagnostic and then failure, without the five-text matrix. Bounded applicability/attribute flags/viewportDraw observations preserve base behavior, and visible/valid/device/model/viewport state is read without show, flag changes or suppression/global settings. No A/B/C retry is retained: v10 actual evidence excluded that timing hypothesis.
+
+Five N9a controls use independently loaded simplex.shx / gbcbig.shx, height 7 and width factor .75. Each control gets a complete, separate 1024x768 and 2048x1536 RGB snapshot with the same 150x112.5 model field. Control-paper conversion is explicitly 150x112.5 mm, 1:1; dpiX/Y are this conversion, not printer specifications. Frame/phase/font/source identity binds each observation. No Layout translation invariance or glyph-complete claim.
+
+Before text, five colored nontext squares at asymmetric, noncollinear positions verify worldToDevice, ATIL upper-left row order, RGB channel conversion and pixel phase. The first three points select only y orientation and {0,.5} center conventions; the other two positions are held out and independently checked. Both groups have a fixed .55 pixel center residual bound. No text fit. All calibration attempts and the selected mapping are written. Unknown mappings fail.
+
+Native links an exact frozen copy of the existing `src/TextOccupancy.cpp` (SHA256 28D106F22219C8CCD6C0FBC9A6C16EC48296177F6DD0A3D1252C3D9ECF5F3520); no algorithm clone or alternate implementation. Files are frozen by `tools/build_text_footprint_gs.ps1` into the build receipt; the receipt is compatible with unchanged native_case_host.py and watch_native_case.py. Run case `NativeGsTextFootprint`; no capture helper or document OPEN needed. Only the independent controller starts/controls CAD.
+
+Outputs: native-case.json, gs-trace.jsonl, gs-result.json, fonts.json; calibration-W.json/.rgb and five ID-W.json/.rgb for each width. Tight RGB is top-to-bottom, three bytes/pixel. The offline verifier checks every nonwhite full cell against the C++ quadrilateral and exact frame mapping, and has shrink/missing-map/wrong-map negative controls. It never supplies buffers to the native command.
+
+Cleanup removes scene/overrule, closes own point, destroys view, restores only its own database association, destroys model/device, releases kernel, then deletes the owned database. An overrule-removal error retains live state and rejects module unload. Ambient write notifications and current/active/working identities are recorded separately. All work remains developer evidence, no production build eligibility.
